{Saunders made a tragic blunder against Mardle. Instead of playing 52 Kh6, when Black has nothing better than the draw by perpetual check he tried} 52. Kf6 Qf4+ {when he had to resign because of} 53. Kxe7 Qf8# {Source: 'Southsea Chess Tournament 1949' by Harry Golombek} 0-1

