{A lively little game which is none the worse for being played in the wrong century. However, I cannot help feeling that if the player of the white pieces had been well acquainted with Morphy's games he would have done better.} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 4. b4 Bxb4 5. c3 Ba5 6. d4 exd4 7. e5 (7. O-O) 7... d5 8. exd6 dxc3 (8... Qxd6 9. O-O Nge7 10. Ng5 O-O 11. Bd3 Bf5 12. Bxf5 Nxf5 13. Ba3 Qg6 14. Bxf8 Qxg5 15. Ba3 dxc3 16. Bc1 Qg6 17. Bf4 Rd8 18. Qe2 Ncd4 19. Qe4 Ng3 $1 20. Qxg6 Nde2# {Marache-Morphy, New York 1857}) 9. O-O Qxd6 10. Qb3 Qf6 11. Bg5 Qf5 12. Re1+ Nge7 13. Bxe7 Nxe7 14. Qa3 $2 ({Stockfish 18:} 14. Re5 $18) 14... Be6 15. Nd4 Qf4 16. Nxe6 fxe6 17. Rxe6 $2 O-O-O 18. Nxc3 Qxc4 19. Rxe7 Qxc3 {Source: 'Southsea Chess Tournament 1949' by Harry Golombek} 0-1

